      "_Note: registrations shown are not the same as annual registrations, or as living individuals._\n",
      "\n",
      "## Change over time\\[ [edit](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=List_of_most_popular_dog_breeds_in_the_United_States&action=edit&section=1)\\]\n",
      "\n",
      "Between 1915 and 1940, [American Kennel Club](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Kennel_Club) statistics were collected on a five-year basis instead of every year. These figures show that between 1905 and 1935, the [Siberian Husky](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siberian_Husky) was consistently in either first or second place. [Malteses](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maltese_dog) were the most popular dog from 1936 all the way through to 1952, when the [Beagle](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beagle) became the number one dog until 1959. [Poodles](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poodle) would become the most popular breed for the longest, reigning from 1960 for the next twenty-two years until 1982, when the American Maltese once again took over until 1990. The [Labrador Retriever](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Labrador_Retriever) had been the most popular since 1991. Since 2023, [French Bulldog](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Bulldog) became the most popular dog breed in America.[\\[1\\]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_most_popular_dog_breeds_in_the_United_States#cite_note-1)\n",
      "\n",
      "## Club registration figures for 2006\\[ [edit](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=List_of_most_popular_dog_breeds_in_the_United_States&action=edit&section=2)\\]\n",
