      "Title: The 50 Most Popular Dog Breeds in the U.S.\n",
      "URL: https://www.countryliving.com/life/kids-pets/g3283/the-50-most-popular-dog-breeds/\n",
      "ID: https://www.countryliving.com/life/kids-pets/g3283/the-50-most-popular-dog-breeds/\n",
      "Score: None\n",
      "Published Date: 2024-12-30T17:57:00.000Z\n",
      "Author: Karla Pope\n",
      "Image: https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/gettyimages-180680638-676f621f720bc.jpg?crop=1.00xw:0.752xh;0,0.118xh&resize=1200:*\n",
      "Favicon: https://www.countryliving.com/_assets/design-tokens/countryliving/static/images/favicon.3bd4cac.ico\n",
      "Extras: None\n",
      "Subpages: None\n",
      "Text: [Skip to Content](https://www.countryliving.com/life/kids-pets/g3283/the-50-most-popular-dog-breeds/#main-content)\n",
      "\n",
      "![Play Icon](https://www.countryliving.com/_assets/design-tokens/fre/static/icons/play.db7c035.svg?primary=%2523ffffff)![preview for 8 Dog Quotes That’ll Melt Your Heart](top&resize=1200:*)\n",
      "\n",
      "Country Living editors select each product featured. If you buy from a link, we may earn a commission. [Why Trust Us?](https://www.countryliving.com/about/a707/contact-us/)\n",
      "\n",
      "Let’s be real: dogs may be the only four-legged members of the family, but they're pretty much always the favorite. And it makes sense that if your fondest memories of growing up are with your springer spaniel, then you just may have a loyalty to that breed well into adulthood. But what breeds have truly stolen the hearts of the rest of America? Every year, the American Kennel Club (AKC) publishes a list of the [most popular dog breeds in America](https://www.akc.org/most-popular-breeds/) based on registration statistics—and you may be surprised to find out who took the top spot.\n",
      "\n",
      "Each year, the AKC list is published after the calendar year has closed and all of the data has been collected and organized. (As of now, the most recent findings we have are from 2023. Results for 2024 will roll in around March, so stay tuned!) If you’re thinking that Labrador retrievers are no. 1, you’d almost be right—they held the title for over three decades—but the new reigning champ is actually the French bulldog. Turns out we can’t get enough of those squishy little faces!\n",
      "\n",
      "Those aren’t the only favorites, of course. The list includes [large dog breeds](https://www.countryliving.com/life/kids-pets/g38962118/largest-dog-breeds/) galore, such as Great Danes and Rottweilers, while sweet and sassy [small dog breeds](https://www.countryliving.com/life/kids-pets/g43679662/small-dog-breeds/) like Shih Tzus and Dachshunds definitely earn bragging rights as well. (One “breed” you won’t find, though, is the Goldendoodle. Why? Because the American Kennel Club focuses on “purebred” dogs, and, as a mix between a Golden retriever and Poodle, Goldendoodles are considered a crossbreed.) So if you’re considering a new pet, you’ll more than likely find your companion on this list of the most popular dog breeds in the U.S. And, just for fun, we threw in a few “on the rise” breeds at the top for consideration as well.\n",
      "\n",
      "**_Check out the_ [Country Living _Pet Lab_](https://www.countryliving.com/life/kids-pets/a60385337/pet-lab/) _and more pet related content:_**\n",
      "\n",
      "- [**The Best Dog Beds for Every Four-Legged Member of Your Family**](https://www.countryliving.com/life/kids-pets/g40971643/best-dog-beds/)\n",
      "- [**The Internet Is Obsessed With This Genius Collapsible Dog Crate**](https://www.countryliving.com/shopping/a42817241/diggs-collapsible-dog-crate/)\n",
      "- [**9 Best Slow Feeder Dog Bowls That Will Actually Pace Your Pet**](https://www.countryliving.com/life/kids-pets/g44938886/best-slow-feeder-dog-bowls/)\n",
      "- [**The Best Pet Cameras**](https://www.countryliving.com/life/kids-pets/g60246991/best-pet-cameras/)\n",
      "\n",
      "1\n",
      "\n",
      "## One to Watch: Great Pyrenees\n",
      "\n",
      "![great pyrenees dog resting from guarding sheep at a mountain farm in north carolina](top&resize=980:*)ejkrouse\n",
      "\n",
      "Inching ever closer to the top 50 are these friendly and cuddly gentle giants, who can weigh over 100 pounds. Their thick, waterproof coat makes them cold-weather friendly, and their mellow persona makes them family-friendly. No wonder they jumped five whole spots on the AKC's most recent ranking!\n",
      "\n",
      "**Related: [Large Dog Breeds to Consider Adopting](https://www.countryliving.com/life/kids-pets/g38962118/largest-dog-breeds/)**\n",
      "\n",
      "2\n",
      "\n",
      "## One to Watch: Finnish Lapphunds\n",
      "\n",
      "![portrait of finnish lapphund dog in nature in summer](top&resize=980:*)LindaE\n",
      "\n",
      "This traditional Nordic herding breed is one of the friendliest you’ll come across—maybe that’s why they jumped up a whopping 32 spots? Speedy and agile with a thick weather-proof coat, Finnish Lapphunds are ideal for active owners who are ready and waiting for a loyal companion. The curved puff tail and spitz-like face only add to the cuteness!\n",
      "\n",
      "**Related: [Dog Breeds that Look Completely Different as Puppies](https://www.countryliving.com/life/kids-pets/a63119129/dog-breeds-look-different-as-puppies/)**\n",
      "\n",
      "Advertisement - Continue Reading Below\n",
      "\n",
      "3\n",
      "\n",
      "## One to Watch: Basenjis\n",
      "\n",
      "![young purebred basenji is posing on the edge of a wood](top&resize=980:*)Photographs by Maria itina\n",
      "\n",
      "This perky little pup just may be the world's oldest documented dog breed! Known as Africa's 'barkless dog' for the unique yodel it produces in lieu of _ruff-ruffs,_ they are fastidious groomers and require an involved owner who will keep up with their training and exercise.\n",
      "\n",
      "**Related: [Best-Behaved Dog Breeds](https://www.countryliving.com/life/kids-pets/a63239614/best-behaved-dog-breeds/)**\n",
      "\n",
      "4\n",
      "\n",
      "## French Bulldogs\n",
      "\n",
      "![view of french bulldog standing on grass most popular dog breeds](0&resize=980:*)Mike Linnane / 500px//Getty Images\n",
      "\n",
      "In 2012, Frenchies ranked at no. 14 on the list. After jumping to the no. 2 spot in 2021, the playful breed took the top spot in 2022, and continues its reign for 2023. Congrats, pal!\n",
      "\n",
      "**Related: [Small Dog Breeds that Stay Tiny Forever](https://www.countryliving.com/life/kids-pets/g43679662/small-dog-breeds/)**\n",
      "\n",
      "Advertisement - Continue Reading Below\n",
      "\n",
      "5\n",
      "\n",
      "## Labrador Retrievers\n",
      "\n",
      "![labrador retriever most popular dog breeds](0&resize=980:*)getty images\n",
      "\n",
      "Having held the title of the most popular dog breed in the U.S. for more than three decades, these lively, all-American pups had the longest reign of any breed. Hey, no. 2 is nothing to sneeze at!\n",
      "\n",
      "**Related: [Labrador Retrievers vs. Golden Retrievers](https://www.countryliving.com/life/kids-pets/a45642197/golden-retriever-vs-labrador-retriever/)**\n",
      "\n",
      "6\n",
      "\n",
      "## Golden Retrievers\n",
      "\n",
      "![golden retriever most popular dog breeds](top&resize=980:*)getty images\n",
      "\n",
      "A friendly, playful sporting dog, golden retrievers are eager, alert, self-confident, and very active and energetic, but they're no watchdogs. This breed is slow to mature, retaining puppy personality for three to four years, which humans may find either delightful or annoying.\n",
      "\n",
      "**Related: [Dog Breeds that Make the Best Companions](https://www.countryliving.com/life/kids-pets/a63160045/best-dog-breeds-companionship/)**\n",
      "\n",
      "Advertisement - Continue Reading Below\n",
      "\n",
      "7\n",
      "\n",
      "## German Shepherds\n",
      "\n",
      "![german shepherd most popular dog breeds](top&resize=980:*)getty images\n",
      "\n",
      "Highly intelligent, seriously loyal, utterly devoted and known for dignity and stature, they can run at great speeds. Buy a heavy duty vacuum if you're bringing one home, as they're nicknamed \"the German Shedder.\"\n",
      "\n",
      "**Related: [Loyal Dogs that Make Great Guard Dogs](https://www.countryliving.com/life/kids-pets/g39559653/best-guard-dogs/)**\n",
      "\n",
      "8\n",
      "\n",
      "## Poodles\n",
      "\n",
      "![poodle most popular dog breeds](0.0420xh&resize=980:*)getty images\n",
      "\n",
      "The national dog of France was originally a hunting dog [from Germany](https://www.britannica.com/animal/poodle). They're good swimmers with waterproof coats, perfect for duck hunting. Their signature fancy haircut is actually a practical protection for joints and vital organs in cold water.\n",
      "\n",
      "Advertisement - Continue Reading Below\n",
      "\n",
      "9\n",
      "\n",
      "## Bulldogs\n",
      "\n",
      "![bulldog most popular dog breeds](top&resize=980:*)getty images\n",
      "\n",
      "Calm, courageous, friendly, affectionate and stubborn, this breed prefers watching TV to taking walks.\n",
      "\n",
      "10\n",
      "\n",
      "## Rottweilers\n",
      "\n",
      "![rottweiler most popular dog breeds](top&resize=980:*)getty images\n",
      "\n",
      "These canines are \"protective, not vicious—they read your cues,\" says Katie Owens of [Atlantahaus Rottweilers](https://www.facebook.com/atlantahaus.rottweilers/), breeders of German Rottweilers since 1979. Although robust and powerful, these pups think they're lap dogs.\n",
      "\n",
      "Advertisement - Continue Reading Below\n",
      "\n",
      "11\n",
      "\n",
      "## Beagles\n",
      "\n",
      "![beagle, most popular dog breeds](0&resize=980:*)getty images\n",
      "\n",
      "A scent hound used primarily to hunt rabbits, beagles are friendly, companionable, and sturdy. They're always curious and tend to follow their noses, which can lead to trouble.\n",
      "\n",
      "12\n",
      "\n",
      "## Dachshunds\n",
      "\n",
      "![dachshunds most popular dog breeds](top&resize=980:*)getty images\n",
      "\n",
      "Playful, brave, and curious, wiener dogs like to dig holes in the yard and chase chipmunks. They're notoriously difficult to housebreak and prefer a covered potty yard for cold or wet weather.\n",
      "\n",
      "**Related: [20 Dog Breeds with Short Legs](https://www.countryliving.com/life/kids-pets/g62261381/dogs-puppies-short-legs/)**\n",
      "\n",
      "Advertisement - Continue Reading Below\n",
      "\n",
      "13\n",
      "\n",
      "## German Shorthaired Pointers\n",
      "\n",
      "![german shorthaired pointer most popular dog breeds](top&resize=980:*)getty images\n",
      "\n",
      "A streamlined, yet powerful, hunting dog with webbed feet, this pooch is best at going after water fowl. GSPs are bold, eccentric, and tenacious, and they can perform all gun dog roles. However, their strong hunting instinct means they may not do so well around other small pets, such as cats or rabbits.\n",
      "\n",
      "14\n",
      "\n",
      "## Pembroke Welsh Corgis\n",
      "\n",
      "![dog breed, dog, carnivore, pembroke welsh corgi, most popular dog breeds](top&resize=980:*)getty images\n",
      "\n",
      "Legend says this breed sprang from [lairs of fairies and elves](https://www.akc.org/expert-advice/lifestyle/fun-facts-about-the-pembroke-welsh-corgi/). PWCs are the smallest herding dog; as such, they'll nip at the heels of kids to herd them and bark at _everything_.\n",
      "\n",
      "Advertisement - Continue Reading Below\n",
      "\n",
      "15\n",
      "\n",
      "## Australian Shepherds\n",
      "\n",
      "![australian shepherd most popular dog breeds](top&resize=980:*)Nicolai Cebotari / 500px//Getty Images\n",
      "\n",
      "What's in a name? Well, this pooch has had many. Bob-Tails, Pastor Dogs, and Blue Heelers are just a few monikers this breed has been called. Known for their different-colored eyes and boundless energy, Aussies make great pets. If you're not a fan of shedding, you might want to rethink bringing one home.\n",
      "\n",
      "**Related: [Which Dog Breed Is the Smartest?](https://www.countryliving.com/life/kids-pets/g45166960/most-intelligent-smart-dog-breeds/)**\n",
      "\n",
      "16\n",
      "\n",
      "## Yorkshire Terriers\n",
      "\n",
      "![dog breed, carnivore, dog, mammal, vertebrate, snout, terrier, small terrier, toy dog, working animal, most popular dog breeds](0&resize=980:*)getty images\n",
      "\n",
      "These six-inch, seven-pound hunting dogs were bred to catch rats and mice that infested clothing mills and mine shafts in Yorkshire, England. With a demeanor that conveys an important air, they're fine companions for adults, but not a good fit for children.\n",
      "\n",
      "Advertisement - Continue Reading Below\n",
      "\n",
      "17\n",
      "\n",
      "## Cavalier King Charles Spaniels\n",
      "\n",
      "![dog breed, vertebrate, dog, carnivore, flower, petal, lavender, purple, toy dog, cavalier king charles spaniel, most popular dog breeds](0&resize=980:*)getty images\n",
      "\n",
      "A sweet-tempered cuddle buddy with an independent streak, this shiny pooch loves to chase squirrels and butterflies. The breed requires lots of attention and isn't happy when left alone.\n",
      "\n",
      "**Related: [Friendliest Dog Breeds that Love to Cuddle](https://www.countryliving.com/life/kids-pets/g63297037/friendly-dog-breeds/)**\n",
      "\n",
      "18\n",
      "\n",
      "## Doberman Pinschers\n",
      "\n",
      "![doberman pinscher most popular dog breeds](0&resize=980:*)getty images\n",
      "\n",
      "Very keen and super energetic, with tremendous strength and stamina, Doberman Pinschers are nonetheless sensitive to cold, and thus, not outdoor dogs. The breed is [the official dog of the U.S. Marine Corps in World War II](https://www.akc.org/expert-advice/dog-breeds/doberman-pinscher-history-surprising-past-behind-breed/); a [Doberman named Cappy](https://www.instagram.com/p/CeLvnwxMTWa/) saved the lives of 250 Marines during the war and became the first K-9 casualty. He was the first dog buried in the National War Dog Cemetery at the Naval Base in Guam.\n",
      "\n",
      "Advertisement - Continue Reading Below\n",
      "\n",
      "19\n",
      "\n",
      "## Boxers\n",
      "\n",
      "![boxer most popular dog breeds](top&resize=980:*)getty images\n",
      "\n",
      "Legend says this breed's name came about because they fight standing on hind legs like a boxer. True or not, they are descendants of an old Tibetan fighting dog and were [pictured on 16th- and 17th-century Flemish tapestries](https://www.akc.org/dog-breeds/boxer/) of stag and boar hunts.\n",
      "\n",
      "20\n",
      "\n",
      "## Miniature Schnauzers\n",
      "\n",
      "![wood, dog, carnivore, dog breed, hardwood, snout, terrier, wood stain, canidae, wood flooring, most popular dog breeds](0&resize=980:*)getty images\n",
      "\n",
      "Weighing in at 10 to 15 pounds, this sturdy dog is affectionate, keen, and docile—but _can_ think he knows more than you. They _must_ be made to heel and follow owner through doors; they make for good watchdogs and vermin hunters.\n",
      "\n",
      "![Headshot of Karla Pope](https://hips.hearstapps.com/rover/profile_photos/322f3f77-e0d5-4be1-8e55-4785b62d8e21_1657125406.file?fill=1:1&resize=120:*)\n",
      "\n",
      "[Karla Pope](https://www.countryliving.com/author/226395/karla-pope/)\n",
      "\n",
      "Karla Pope is a longtime writer, editor and blogger with more than two decades of editorial experience. She’s written for a variety of outlets including _Good Housekeeping_, _Woman’s Day_, _Travel + Leisure_, Tripadvisor, _People_, _Parade_ and more. Her coverage includes travel, lifestyle, entertainment and wellness content. When she's not exploring the world with her family, you can find her curled up on the couch watching a documentary and eating gummy bears.\n",
      "\n",
      "Advertisement - Continue Reading Below\n",
      "\n",
